        "comments": "The assembly drAceMons1.hap1.1 is based on 60x PacBio data and Arima2 Hi-C data generated by the Ancient Environmental Genomics Initiative for Sustainability (AEGIS,\nhttps://globe.ku.dk/research/ancient-environmental-genomics-initiative-for-sustainability). The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio assembly generation with Hifiasm in Hi-C integrated assembly mode, and Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHS. The mitochondrial and plastid genomes were assembled using OATK. Finally, each haplotype assembly was analysed and manually improved using TreeVal. Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by the Hi-C data have been named in order of size. Some haplotipic inversions were observed on: Chromosome 1 12.62 Mbp - 31.11 Mbp and 36.60 Mbp - 39.47 Mbp, Chromosome 8 17.95 Mbp - 20.60 Mbp, Chromosome 9 14.06 Mbp - 26.83 Mbp, Chromosome 11 14.80 Mbp - 24.45 Mbp and Chromosome 13 25.41 Mbp - 28.83 Mbp. There is a chromosome rearrangement on Chromosome 7 10.37 Mbp - 12.85 Mbp when compared to HAP2.",
